  "brand": "Adidas",
  "size": "XL",
  "comment": "Shearer 9. Replica",
  "story": "Newcastle United's 1997/98 Adidas away shirt had a navy base lifted by orange and green, with a single bold vertical stripe in green and amber running down the front and a large Newcastle Brown Ale sponsor logo. It is now remembered mainly through the club's 2025/26 third shirt, which Adidas and the club presented as a modern tribute borrowing the navy, burnt orange and deep green of the 97/98 kit while dropping the stripe and oversized sponsor. The shirt belongs to Kenny Dalglish's only full season in charge: Newcastle played in the Champions League group stage, beat Barcelona 3-2 at home with a Faustino Asprilla hat-trick, finished 13th in the Premier League and lost the FA Cup final 2-0 to Arsenal. The club's own announcement calls it both the 97/98 away and the 97/98 third kit.",
  "sources": [
   "https://www.footyheadlines.com/2024/11/newcastle-25-26-away-kit.html",
   "https://www.newcastleunited.com/en/news/adidas-and-newcastle-united-reveal-2025-26-third-jersey",
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1997%E2%80%9398_Newcastle_United_F.C._season"
  ],
