  "size": "XL",
  "story": "Newcastle's 1994/95 third shirt was an Asics design in green with thin dark blue stripes, carrying the McEwan's Lager sponsor and the polo collar shared by the club's Asics shirts of 1993-95. It existed because the black-and-white home and the blue away kit both clashed with Sheffield Wednesday, and it was worn in competitive football only twice, both times at Hillsborough: a 1-0 win in March 1994 and a 0-0 draw in January 1995. Museum of Jerseys notes the look resembled Leeds United's third kit of the same period, but no source read says the design was deliberately inspired by anything.",
