  "story": "Germany's adidas home kit for the 2014 World Cup was all white, with a chest graphic in several shades of red that adidas presented as an interpretation of the German flag; three stars above the crest marked the 1954, 1974 and 1990 titles, and details such as the new DFB logo were done in silver. Adidas designer Jürgen Rank explained the all-white look as standing for the lightness of the German game, and the kit was first worn in a friendly against Italy in Milan in November 2013. Germany wore it in the final on 13 July 2014 at the Maracanã, beating Argentina 1-0 after extra time through Mario Götze's 113th-minute goal. Adidas later said the shirt had sold more than 3 million units, a record for a Germany shirt, with a four-star version issued after the win.",
