  "story": "The 2008/09 Étoile Sportive du Sahel home shirt is an all-red adidas shirt with the three white stripes along the shoulders, white trim on the collar and cuffs, and a dotted white panel down each side. The chest carries the Tunisie Telecom logo with a second \"Saïd\" wordmark below it, the adidas logo on the right and the club's small red crest with its white five-pointed star on the left; the red-and-white scheme and the star go back to the club's founding and reference the Tunisian flag. The club finished third in the Tunisian league that season and went out of the cup in the quarter-finals, 1-0 to Espérance, a run that ended Gernot Rohr's spell as coach. Wikipedia's supplier table lists Diadora for 2006-09, but the shirt photographed by Classic Football Shirts is adidas.",
